RTIAL.** WI-828 delivered none of its","+Done-when. The lane branch adds only the handback and the spec move. The squash","+`e925bebb8` adds bookkeeping: the generated state, `status.md`, the needs of","+WI-833/WI-850/WI-851 re-pointed, and WI-892's spec widened. No code and no spine","+row changed. COMPLETE would be wrong. CANCELLED would also be wrong: the ask","+still stands and waits on an owner ruling (OI-113), and the lane did not decide","+it should never ship. The one route that would retire it, OI-113 option (d),","+is the owner's to choose and is not chosen.","+","+**2. The keep/discard split is honest.** Both lists are empty, and the range is","+empty, so nothing of the lane's work stays on trunk. The round-1 diff is","+outside the repository (`C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/wi-828-round1-parked.patch`,","+25,450 bytes, present). It is neither a keep nor a discard left on trunk. It is","+an off-record artifact that two queued specs cite (finding 4).","+","+**3. The successor already exists, and the existing rows carry the substance.**","+WI-893 is queued with `needs = [\"OI-113\", \"WI-892\"]` and","+`specref = \"docs/requirements/open-items.toml#OI-113\"`. That is the placeholder","+shape an `[open_item]` mint would have produced. OI-113 is `pending` and carries","+all four cells (`one_line`, `blast_radius`, `options` (a)–(d) and","+`recommendation` (a)). That is the owner card I would have written: the trunk","+identity the walk needs is a design choice with adopter-facing cost, so it is","+the owner's. No queued row still `needs` WI-828; the squash re-pointed","+WI-833/WI-850/WI-851 to WI-892 by hand. So the edge re-point a mint would make","+is already done. Drafting a `## Dispositions` block here would mint a second","+queued row for the same scope, both behind OI-113 and both answering SR-140.","+That duplicate is worse than every gap below, so I drafted none.","+","+One part of the substance is missing: lineage. WI-893 carries no `supersedes`,","+so nothing joins WI-828 to its continuation across the id change.","+","+**4. WI-828's ask continues in two rows, not one.** The report's \"Not","+delivered\" says the whole Done-when goes to WI-893. The squash's own message","+and diff say otherwise. Done-when bullet 1's shared walk (\"the hook's one","+lane-commit walk ... so later per-commit checks ride the same walk\") went to","+WI-892: its title and Done-when gained \"one lane-commit walk with a rider","+tuple\". Only the hand-merge path (`HEAD..MERGE_HEAD`) went to WI-893. The report","+is immutable, so this verdict is where the corrected thread is recorded.","+","+- [MAJOR] WI-893 lacks `supersedes` -> a disposition's successor must carry it so partial work keeps its thread across the id change, and without it nothing links WI-828 to the row continuing its hand-merge ask -> add the top-level frontmatter line `supersedes = \"WI-828\"` (a bare string) to the `+++` block of `docs/work/queued/WI-893-hand-merge-walk-per-oi-113.md`; `supersedes` is a registry column (`kitlib/registry.py`), and for a `partial` predecessor the lineage check (`check_trajectory.py` `_restructured_lineage_findings`) asks nothing back of WI-828, so WI-828 stays byte-identical -> @owner","+- [MAJOR] this row's mechanical close will be REFUSED -> `handback.py` (the `owes_successor` guard near line 870) refuses a disposition row whose `## Dispositions` holds no TOML draft and stops the run for a human; no draft key names an EXISTING queued row (`intake._DRAFT_KEYS` mints a new row only) -> close WI-894 by hand, citing this verdict and naming WI-893 as the successor once it carries `supersedes`; separately, file the missing arm as its own WI (for example a draft that adopts an existing queued row by id, so a hand-filed successor discharges a disposition without a duplicate). This is a gap in the machinery, not a defect of this lane -> @owner","+- [MINOR] the report attributes the whole unfinished Done-when to WI-893 -> the shared lane-commit wal